1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,147
ScopedAct checks an AI agent’s requests before protected tools execute. This walkthrough uses actual

2
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:10,293
console screenshots and recorded local evaluations. It is an edited explanation of saved runs,

3
00:00:10,293 --> 00:00:15,440
not a continuous live recording.

4
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:22,392
To try it yourself, download the source and follow the native review guide. Install

5
00:00:22,392 --> 00:00:27,845
Python and Ollama, download the local model, and install ScopedAct. Run the native review

6
00:00:27,845 --> 00:00:33,298
launcher. It opens a private localhost console link. Keep the terminal open while reviewing.

7
00:00:33,298 --> 00:00:38,750
This native mode does not provide Docker network isolation.

8
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:46,203
The lab models a staging login incident. The reviewer selects a simulated role. The

9
00:00:46,203 --> 00:00:52,157
intern can read diagnostics. The responder can also inspect configuration and propose changes for

10
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:58,110
approval. These are local evaluation profiles, not enterprise identity integration.

11
00:00:59,610 --> 00:01:05,603
In the recorded intern evaluation, the agent read login events and deployment history. Its

12
00:01:05,603 --> 00:01:11,597
next request attempted to read authentication configuration. ScopedAct denied that request because the task

13
00:01:11,597 --> 00:01:17,590
did not grant permission. The protected connector did not execute it.

14
00:01:19,090 --> 00:01:24,053
The runner paused at the denial, before the remaining queued call could execute. One

15
00:01:24,053 --> 00:01:29,015
queued call was discarded. The operator continued with unchanged permissions. The model then finished

16
00:01:29,015 --> 00:01:33,978
without making another request. Ending the evaluation revoked the task. This pauses this runner,

17
00:01:33,978 --> 00:01:38,940
not every independent client.

18
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:46,163
The activity map groups actual requests by agent and resource. Request numbers show the

19
00:01:46,163 --> 00:01:51,887
observed order. Expand a resource to inspect its decision and execution record. A blocked

20
00:01:51,887 --> 00:01:57,610
resource is not a simulated warning, and the map does not invent agent reasoning.

21
00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:05,217
A separate responder evaluation read four permitted resources, but the model misinterpreted configuration evidence

22
00:02:05,217 --> 00:02:11,323
and proposed no repair. Authorization controls do not guarantee a correct diagnosis. This limitation

23
00:02:11,323 --> 00:02:17,430
remains visible rather than being replaced with a staged successful outcome.

24
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:25,510
Review ScopedAct as a developer preview. Challenge the permission boundary, revocation, delegation constraints, and

25
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:32,090
execution evidence. The source and draft review are available on GitHub at jgoradia3 slash

26
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:38,670
scopedact. This local lab uses synthetic data and does not connect to production.
